-- title:
--   An L-automorphism exchanging the two minimal primes over varpi
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible via $L$. Let $j \in K$, non-zero, whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under `coeffEmb`. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ such that: for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ whose members are exactly the $f$ admitting a presentation $f \cdot y = x$ with $x, y$ power series over $A$ and $y$ of non-zero reduction modulo the maximal ideal (the Gauss condition), the pull-back $\sigma^{-1}(W_0)$ is different from $W_0$, and for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ of non-zero reduction both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $\sigma^{-1}(W_0)$. Let $\rho_\sigma$ be a ring automorphism of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K j` — the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ — inducing $\sigma$ on underlying elements. Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ satisfying the Gauss condition above, and let $\mathfrak{P}_0 \ne \mathfrak{P}_1$ be minimal primes of $\varpi$ times the chart algebra, with $\mathfrak{P}_0$ consisting of the elements whose image in $K$ is a non-unit of $W_0$. Then $\rho_\sigma^{-1}(\mathfrak{P}_0) = \mathfrak{P}_1$ and $\rho_\sigma^{-1}(\mathfrak{P}_1) = \mathfrak{P}_0$.
--
--   This is the algebraic form of the statement that the automorphism attached to the level-$p$ structure interchanges the two Igusa components of the special fibre of the integral two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$: the two minimal primes over a uniformiser are the centres of the two Gauss-type valuation subrings, and an $L$-automorphism moving one of them must swap them. It feeds the analysis of the special fibre of the two-chart model and of the induced map on its two branches.
